e\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"In these cases, Cursor falls back to a compatible model. If you're seeing unexpected model behavior, check your plan and model settings.\"}]\n62:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"code\":\"---\\nname: code-reviewer\\ndescription: Reviews code for correctness and style.\\nmodel: inherit\\n---\\n\\nReview the code changes for bugs, style issues, and edge cases.\",\"language\":\"markdown\",\"title\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb8\",null,{\"language\":\"markdown\",\"children\":\"---\\nname: code-reviewer\\ndescription: Reviews code for correctness and style.\\nmodel: inherit\\n---\\n\\nReview the code changes for bugs, style issues, and edge cases.\"}]}]}]\n63:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"code\":\"---\\nname: search-agent\\ndescription: Searches the codebase for relevant files and symbols.\\nmodel: inherit\\n---\\n\\nSearch the codebase and return relevant file paths and code snippets.\",\"language\":\"markdown\",\"title\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb8\",null,{\"language\":\"markdown\",\"children\":\"---\\nname: search-agent\\ndescription: Searches the codebase for relevant files and symbols.\\nmodel: inherit\\n---\\n\\nSearch the codebase and return relevant file paths and code snippets.\"}]}]}]\n64:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"code\":\"---\\nname: reasoning-agent\\ndescription: Handles complex architectural decisions.\\nm"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"odel: gpt-5.6-sol\\n---\\n\\nAnalyze the architecture and recommend changes with detailed reasoning.\",\"language\":\"markdown\",\"title\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb8\",null,{\"language\":\"markdown\",\"children\":\"---\\nname: reasoning-agent\\ndescription: Handles complex architectural decisions.\\nmodel: gpt-5.6-sol\\n---\\n\\nAnalyze the architecture and recommend changes with detailed reasoning.\"}]}]}]\n65:[\"$\",\"$Lb3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Parent model and usage pools\"}]\n66:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"The model picker, including Auto, applies to the parent agent. A subagent can run a different model:\"}]\n67:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 prose-ul-markers\",\"style\":{\"listStyleType\":\"square\",\"listStylePosition\":\"outside\",\"paddingLeft\":\"calc(4rem / 3)\",\"lineHeight\":\"1.5\"},\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":\"Built-in subagents (Explore, Bash, Browser) pick a model for the subtask.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[\"Custom subagents use \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\"inherit\"}],\" or the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\"model\"}],\" field in frontmatter.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":\"The parent agent can name a model when it launches a subagent.\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n68:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Each request bills at the list price of the model that ran. A named third-party model draws from the \",[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"/docs/models-and-pricing#other-models\",\"children\":\"Other Models\"}],\" pool, including when the parent chat is on Auto, Grok, or Composer. On Teams and Enterprise, third-party requests also incur the \",[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"/docs/models-and-pricing#cursor-token-rate\",\"children\":\"Cursor Token Rate\"}],\".\"]}]\n69:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"The subagent task card shows which model ran. The \",[\"$\",\"$Lbe\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"https://cursor.com/dashboard/usage\",\"children\":\"usage dashboard\"}],\" lists that model on the matching usage row.\"]}]\n6a:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Team admins can block models for the team from \",[\"$\",\"$Lbe\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"https://cursor.com/dashboard/team-settings/models\",\"children\":\"Team Settings \u003e Models\"}],\". See \",[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"/docs/enterprise/model-and-integration-management#model-access-control\",\"children\":\"model access control\"}],\".\"]}]\n6b:[\"$\",\"$Lb3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Using subagents\"}]\n6c:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Automatic delegation\"}]\n6d:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"Agent proactively delegates tasks based on:\"}]\n6e:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 prose-ul-markers\",\"style\":{\"listStyleType\":\"square\",\"listStylePosition\":\"outside\",\"paddingLeft\":\"calc(4rem / 3)\",\"lineHeight\":\"1.5\"},\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fon"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"tSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":\"The task complexity and scope\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":\"Custom subagent descriptions in your project\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":\"Current context and available tools\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n6f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"Include phrases like \\\"use proactively\\\" or \\\"always use for\\\" in your description field to encourage automatic delegation.\"}]\n70:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Explicit invocation\"}]\n71:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Request a specific subagent by using the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\"/name\"}],\" syntax in your prompt:\"]}]\n72:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"code\":\"\u003e /verifier confirm the auth flow is complete\\n\u003e /debugger investigate this error\\n\u003e /security-auditor review the payment module\",\"language\":\"text\",\"title\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb8\",null,{\"language\":\"text\",\"children\":\"\u003e /verifier confirm the auth flow is complete\\n\u003e /debugger investigate this error\\n\u003e /security-auditor review the payment module\"}]}]}]\n73:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"You can also invoke subagents by mentioning them naturally:\"}]\n74:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"code\":\"\u003e Use the verifier subagent to confirm the auth flow is complete\\n\u003e Have the debugger subagent investigate this error\\n\u003e Run the security-auditor subagent on the payment module\",\"language\":\"text\",\"title\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb8\",null,{\"language\":\"text\",\"children\":\"\u003e Use the verifier subagent to confirm the auth flow is complete\\n\u003e Have the debugger subagent investigate this error\\n\u003e Run the security-auditor subagent on the payment module\"}]}]}]\n75:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Parallel execution\"}]\n76:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"Launch multiple subagents concurrently for maximum throughput:\"}]\n77:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"code\":\"\u003e Review the API changes and update the documentation in parallel\",\"language\":\"text\",\"title\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb8\",null,{\"language\":\"text\",\"children\":\"\u003e Review the API changes and update the documentation in parallel\"}]}]}]\n78:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"Agent sends multiple Task tool calls in a single message, so subagents run simultaneously.\"}]\n79:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Isolated project copies\"}]\n7a:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"Subagents share the parent agent's checkout by default. When several subagents edit files at once, they can overwrite each other's changes. Ask for isolation and each subagent runs in its own copy of the project:\"}]\n7b:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"code\":\"\u003e Run a swarm of subagents to fix these five flaky tests, each in its own environment\",\"language\":\"text\",\"title\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb8\",null,{\"language\":\"text\",\"children\":\"\u003e Run a swarm of subagents to fix these five flaky tests, each in its own environment\"}]}]}]\n7c:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"Each subagent gets its own environment with its own branch: an isolated Git worktree with a separate working directory on the same machine, or its own cloud environment with a dedicated VM and clone of the repository. Changes stay on each subagent's branch until the parent agent merges the results.\"}]\n7d:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"This is subagent-level i"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"solation within one session. To isolate a whole agent instead, run it in a \",[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"/docs/configuration/worktrees\",\"children\":\"worktree\"}],\", or hand the task to a \",[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"#cloud-subagents\",\"children\":\"cloud subagent\"}],\".\"]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"$Lb3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Cloud subagents\"}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"From a local agent session, you can hand off work to a cloud subagent that runs on its own VM and branch. Your local workspace stays clean and responsive while long-running or parallel work happens in the cloud. The parent agent keeps running locally or in the cloud without interruption. Cloud subagents run from the \",[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"/docs/agent/agents-window\",\"children\":\"Agents Window\"}],\" in the Cursor desktop app.\"]}]\n80:[\"$\",\"$Lbf\",null,{\"playbackId\":\"4ZTyAo008b68KOgo6OijUvPmBHdHLN9d02n8wqlZMRekI\"}]\n81:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Start a cloud subagent with /in-cloud\"}]\n82:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Type \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\"/in-cloud\"}],\" and the next task you submit runs as a cloud subagent. It spins up its own VM and branch to work on the task.\"]}]\n83:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"This is useful for isolating long-running or parallel work, such as fixing CI, investigating an issue, or exploring a codebase while you keep working locally.\"}]\n84:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Put a PR on autopilot with /autopilot\"}]\n85:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Ask a cloud subagent to take over a pull request with \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\"/autopilot\"}],\" or by clicking the quick-action pill. The cloud agent iterates remotely to prepare the PR for merge without tying up your local session.\"]}]\n86:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Cloud subagents use the \",[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"/docs/cloud-agent/setup\",\"children\":\"environment\"}],\" configured for your repo and follow the same model and capability rules as other \",[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"/docs/cloud-agent\",\"children\":\"Cloud Agents\"}],\". Because they run on a cloud VM, their \",[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"/docs/cloud-agent/capabilities#mcp-tools\",\"children\":\"MCP servers\"}],\" come from your team's configuration at \",[\"$\",\"$Lbe\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"https://cursor.com/agents\",\"children\":\"cursor.com/agents\"}],\", not from your local session.\"]}]\n87:[\"$\",\"$Lb3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Resuming subagents\"}]\n88:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"Subagents can be resumed to continue previous conversations. This is useful for long-running tasks that span multiple invocations.\"}]\n89:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\""])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"Each subagent execution returns an agent ID. Pass this ID to resume the subagent with full context preserved:\"}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"code\":\"\u003e Resume agent abc123 and analyze the remaining test failures\",\"language\":\"text\",\"title\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb8\",null,{\"language\":\"text\",\"children\":\"\u003e Resume agent abc123 and analyze the remaining test failures\"}]}]}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative grid w-full grid-cols-[0_1fr] gap-y-0.5 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-sm has-[\u003esvg]:grid-cols-[calc(var(--spacing)*4)_1fr] has-[\u003esvg]:gap-x-3 [\u0026\u003esvg]:size-4 [\u0026\u003esvg]:translate-y-0.5 [\u0026\u003esvg]:text-current bg-card text-card-foreground my-6 items-center\",\"data-slot\":\"alert\",\"role\":\"alert\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-info h-4 w-4 mb-1\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"circle\",\"1mglay\",{\"cx\":\"12\",\"cy\":\"12\",\"r\":\"10\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"1dtifu\",{\"d\":\"M12 16v-4\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"e9boi3\",{\"d\":\"M12 8h.01\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"col-start-2 grid justify-items-start gap-1 text-muted-foreground text-sm [\u0026_p]:mb-0 [\u0026_p]:leading-relaxed\",\"data-slot\":\"alert-description\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"Background subagents write their state as they run. You can resume a subagent after it completes to continue the conversation with preserved context.\"}]}]]}]\n8c:[\"$\",\"$Lb3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Common patterns\"}]\n8d:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Verification agent\"}]\n8e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"A verification agent independently validates whether claimed work was actually completed. This addresses a common issue where AI marks tasks as done but implementations are incomplete or broken.\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8f:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"code\":\"---\\nname: verifier\\ndescription: Validates completed work. Use after tasks are marked done to confirm implementations are functional.\\n---\\n\\nYou are a skeptical validator. Your job is to verify that work claimed as complete actually works.\\n\\nWhen invoked:\\n1. Identify what was claimed to be completed\\n2. Check that the implementation exists and is functional\\n3. Run relevant tests or verification steps\\n4. Look for edge cases that may have been missed\\n\\nBe thorough and skeptical. Report:\\n- What was verified and passed\\n- What was claimed but incomplete or broken\\n- Specific issues that need to be addressed\\n\\nDo not accept claims at face value. Test everything.\",\"language\":\"markdown\",\"title\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb8\",null,{\"language\":\"markdown\",\"children\":\"---\\nname: verifier\\ndescription: Validates completed work. Use after tasks are marked done to confirm implementations are functional.\\n---\\n\\nYou are a skeptical validator. Your job is to verify that work claimed as complete actually works.\\n\\nWhen invoked:\\n1. Identify what was claimed to be completed\\n2. Check that the implementation exists and is functional\\n3. Run relevant tests or verification steps\\n4. Look for edge cases that may have been missed\\n\\nBe thorough and skeptical. Report:\\n- What was verified and passed\\n- What was claimed but incomplete or broken\\n- Specific issues that need to be addressed\\n\\nDo not accept claims at face value. Test everything.\"}]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"90:[\"$\",\"$Lb5\",null,{\"type\":\"prompt\",\"text\":\"Create a subagent file at .cursor/agents/verifier.md with YAML frontmatter containing name and description. The description should be 'Validates completed work. Use after tasks are marked done to confirm implementations are functional.' The prompt body should instruct it to be skeptical, verify implementations actually work by running tests, and look for edge cases.\"}]\n91:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"This pattern is useful for:\"}]\n92:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 prose-ul-markers\",\"style\":{\"listStyleType\":\"square\",\"listStylePosition\":\"outside\",\"paddingLeft\":\"calc(4rem / 3)\",\"lineHeight\":\"1.5\"},\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":\"Validating that features work end-to-end before marking tickets complete\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":\"Catching partially implemented functionality\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":\"Ensuring tests actually pass (not just that test files exist)\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n93:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Orchestrator pattern\"}]\n94:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"For complex workflows, a parent agent can coordinate multiple specialist subagents in sequence:\"}]\n95:[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4 prose-ol-markers\",\"style\":{\"listStyleType\":\"decimal\",\"listStylePosition\":\"outside\",\"paddingLeft\":\"calc(4rem / 3)\",\"lineHeight\":\"1.5\"},\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Planner\"}],\" analyzes requirements and creates a technical plan\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Implementer\"}],\" builds the feature based on the plan\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Verifier\"}],\" confirms the implementation matches requirements\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n96:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"Each handoff includes structured output so the next agent has clear context.\"}]\n97:[\"$\",\"$Lb3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Example subagents\"}]\n98:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Debugger\"}]\n99:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"code\":\"---\\nname: debugger\\ndescription: Debugging specialist for errors and test failures. Use when encountering issues.\\n---\\n\\nYou are an expert debugger specializing in root cause analysis.\\n\\nWhen invoked:\\n1. Capture error message and stack trace\\n2. Identify reproduction steps\\n3. Isolate the failure location\\n4. Implement minimal fix\\n5. Verify solution works\\n\\nFor each issue, provide:\\n- Root cause explanation\\n- Evidence supporting the diagnosis\\n- Specific code fix\\n- Testing approach\\n\\nFocus on fixing the underlying issue, not symptoms.\",\"language\":\"markdown\",\"title\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb8\",null,{\"language\":\"markdown\",\"children\":\"---\\nname: debugger\\ndescription: Debugging specialist for errors and test failures. Use when encountering issues.\\n---\\n\\nYou are an expert debugger specializing in root cause analysis.\\n\\nWhen invoked:\\n1. Capture error message and stack trace\\n2. Identify reproduction steps\\n3. Isolate the failure location\\n4. Implement minimal fix\\n5. Verify solution works\\n\\nFor each issue, provide:\\n- Root cause explanation\\n- Evidence supporting the diagnosis\\n- Specific code fix\\n- Testing approach\\n\\nFocus on fixing the underlying issue, not symptoms.\"}]}]}]\n9a:[\"$\",\"$Lb5\",null,{\"type\":\"prompt\",\"text\":\"Create a subagent file at .cursor/agents/debugger.md with YAML frontmatter containing name and desc"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ription. The debugger subagent should specialize in root cause analysis: capture stack traces, identify reproduction steps, isolate failures, implement minimal fixes, and verify solutions.\"}]\n9b:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Test runner\"}]\n9c:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"code\":\"---\\nname: test-runner\\ndescription: Test automation expert. Use proactively to run tests and fix failures.\\n---\\n\\nYou are a test automation expert.\\n\\nWhen you see code changes, proactively run appropriate tests.\\n\\nIf tests fail:\\n1. Analyze the failure output\\n2. Identify the root cause\\n3. Fix the issue while preserving test intent\\n4. Re-run to verify\\n\\nReport test results with:\\n- Number of tests passed/failed\\n- Summary of any failures\\n- Changes made to fix issues\",\"language\":\"markdown\",\"title\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb8\",null,{\"language\":\"markdown\",\"children\":\"---\\nname: test-runner\\ndescription: Test automation expert. Use proactively to run tests and fix failures.\\n---\\n\\nYou are a test automation expert.\\n\\nWhen you see code changes, proactively run appropriate tests.\\n\\nIf tests fail:\\n1. Analyze the failure output\\n2. Identify the root cause\\n3. Fix the issue while preserving test intent\\n4. Re-run to verify\\n\\nReport test results with:\\n- Number of tests passed/failed\\n- Summary of any failures\\n- Changes made to fix issues\"}]}]}]\n9d:[\"$\",\"$Lb5\",null,{\"type\":\"prompt\",\"text\":\"Create a subagent file at .cursor/agents/test-runner.md with YAML frontmatter containing name and description (mentioning 'Use proactively'). The test-runner subagent should proactively run tests when it sees code changes, analyze failures, fix issues while preserving test intent, and report results.\"}]\n9e:[\"$\",\"$Lb3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Best practices\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"9f:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 prose-ul-markers\",\"style\":{\"listStyleType\":\"square\",\"listStylePosition\":\"outside\",\"paddingLeft\":\"calc(4rem / 3)\",\"lineHeight\":\"1.5\"},\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Write focused subagents\"}],\" — Each subagent should have a single, clear responsibility. Avoid generic \\\"helper\\\" agents.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Invest in descriptions\"}],\" — The \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\"description\"}],\" field determines when Agent delegates to your subagent. Spend time refining it. Test by making prompts and checking if the right subagent gets triggered.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Keep prompts concise\"}],\" — Long, rambling prompts dilute focus. Be specific and direct.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Add subagents to version control\"}],\" — Check \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\".cursor/agents/\"}],\" into your repository so the team benefits.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Start with Agent-generated agents\"}],\" — Let Agent help you draft the initial configuration, then customize.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Use hooks for file output\"}],\" — If you need subagents to produce structured output files, consider using \",[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"/docs/hooks\",\"children\":\"hooks\"}],\" to process and save their results consistently.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a0:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Anti-patterns to avoid\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a1:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative grid w-full grid-cols-[0_1fr] gap-y-0.5 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 text-sm has-[\u003esvg]:grid-cols-[calc(var(--spacing)*4)_1fr] has-[\u003esvg]:gap-x-3 [\u0026\u003esvg]:size-4 [\u0026\u003esvg]:translate-y-0.5 [\u0026\u003esvg]:text-current text-card-foreground my-6 items-center border-yellow-200 bg-yellow-50 dark:border-yellow-700 dark:bg-yellow-900/20\",\"data-slot\":\"alert\",\"role\":\"alert\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-triangle-alert h-4 w-4 mb-1 text-yellow-600 dark:text-yellow-400\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"wmoenq\",{\"d\":\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"juzpu7\",{\"d\":\"M12 9v4\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"p32p05\",{\"d\":\"M12 17h.01\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],\"$undefined\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"col-start-2 grid justify-items-start gap-1 text-sm [\u0026_p]:mb-0 [\u0026_p]:leading-relaxed text-yellow-700 dark:text-yellow-300\",\"data-slot\":\"alert-description\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Don't create dozens of generic subagents.\"}],\" Having 50+ subagents with vague instructions like \\\"helps with coding\\\" is ineffective. Agent won't know when to use them, and you'll waste time maintaining them.\"]}]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a2:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 prose-ul-markers\",\"style\":{\"listStyleType\":\"square\",\"listStylePosition\":\"outside\",\"paddingLeft\":\"calc(4rem / 3)\",\"lineHeight\":\"1.5\"},\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Vague descriptions\"}],\" — \\\"Use for general tasks\\\" gives Agent no signal about when to delegate. Be specific: \\\"Use when implementing authentication flows with OAuth providers.\\\"\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Overly long prompts\"}],\" — A 2,000-word prompt doesn't make a subagent smarter. It makes it slower and harder to maintain.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Duplicating slash commands\"}],\" — If a task is single-purpose and doesn't need context isolation, use a \",[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"/docs/skills\",\"children\":\"skill\"}],\" or \",[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"/docs/customize-cursor#extension-components\",\"children\":\"command\"}],\" instead.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Too many subagents\"}],\" — Start with 2-3 focused subagents. Add more only when you have clear, distinct use cases.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"a3:[\"$\",\"$Lb3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Managing subagents\"}]\na4:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Creating subagents\"}]\na5:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"The easiest way to create a subagent is to ask Agent to create one for you:\"}]\na6:[\"$\",\"$Lb5\",null,{\"type\":\"prompt\",\"text\":\"Create a subagent file at .cursor/agents/security-reviewer.md with YAML frontmatter containing name and description. The security-reviewer subagent should check code for common vulnerabilities like injection, XSS, and hardcoded secrets.\"}]\na7:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"You can also create subagents manually by adding markdown files to \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\".cursor/agents/\"}],\" (project) or \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\"~/.cursor/agents/\"}],\" (user).\"]}]\na8:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Viewing subagents\"}]\na9:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Agent includes all custom subagents in its available tools. You can see which subagents are configured by checking the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\".cursor/agents/\"}],\" directory in your project.\"]}]\naa:[\"$\",\"$Lb3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Performance and cost\"}]\nab:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"Subagents have trade-offs. Understanding them helps you decide when to use them.\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ac:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"full-width-table\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-sm border dark:border-muted\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"table\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-full divide-y divide-neutral-200 bg-card dark:divide-muted dark:bg-card\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"thead\",null,{\"className\":\"dark:text-neutral-300\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3 text-left font-medium text-xs\",\"scope\":\"col\",\"children\":\"Benefit\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-3 text-left font-medium text-xs\",\"scope\":\"col\",\"children\":\"Trade-off\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"tbody\",null,{\"className\":\"divide-y divide-neutral-200 bg-background dark:divide-muted\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-neutral-900 text-base dark:text-neutral-100 [\u0026:first-child_code]:whitespace-nowrap\",\"children\":\"Context isolation\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-neutral-900 text-base dark:text-neutral-100 [\u0026:first-child_code]:whitespace-nowrap\",\"children\":\"Startup overhead (each subagent gathers its own context)\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-neutral-900 text-base dark:text-neutral-100 [\u0026:first-child_code]:whitespace-nowrap\",\"children\":\"Parallel execution\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-neutral-900 text-base dark:text-neutral-100 [\u0026:first-child_code]:whitespace-nowrap\",\"children\":\"Higher token usage (multiple contexts running simultaneously)\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-neutral-900 text-base dark:text-neutral-100 [\u0026:first-child_code]:whitespace-nowrap\",\"children\":\"Specialized focus\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 text-neutral-900 text-base dark:text-neutral-100 [\u0026:first-child_code]:whitespace-nowrap\",\"children\":\"Latency (may be slower than main agent for simple tasks)\"}]]}]]}]]}]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ad:[\"$\",\"$Lb4\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3\",\"children\":\"Token and cost considerations\"}]\nae:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 prose-ul-markers\",\"style\":{\"listStyleType\":\"square\",\"listStylePosition\":\"outside\",\"paddingLeft\":\"calc(4rem / 3)\",\"lineHeight\":\"1.5\"},\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Subagents consume tokens independently\"}],\" — Each subagent has its own context window and token usage. Running five subagents in parallel uses roughly five times the tokens of a single agent.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Evaluate the overhead\"}],\" — For quick, simple tasks, the main agent is often faster. Subagents shine for complex, long-running, or parallel work.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"style\":{\"paddingInlineStart\":\"4px\",\"margin\":\"0 0 0.5rem 0\",\"fontSize\":\"15px\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Subagents can be slower\"}],\" — The benefit is context isolation, not speed. A subagent doing a simple task may be slower than the main agent because it starts fresh.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\naf:[\"$\",\"$Lb3\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 mb-4\",\"children\":\"FAQ\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"b0:[\"$\",\"$Lc0\",null,{\"className\":\"$undefined\",\"collapsible\":true,\"type\":\"single\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lc1\",\"What are the built-in subagents?\",{\"value\":\"What are the built-in subagents?\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lc2\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"What are the built-in subagents?\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"$Lc3\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Cursor includes three built-in subagents: \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\"explore\"}],\" for codebase search, \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\"bash\"}],\" for running shell commands, and \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\"browser\"}],\" for browser automation via MCP. These handle context-heavy operations automatically. You don't need to configure them.\"]}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$Lc1\",\"Can subagents launch other subagents?\",{\"value\":\"Can subagents launch other subagents?\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lc2\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Can subagents launch other subagents?\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"$Lc3\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"Yes, within a nesting limit. Since Cursor 2.5, subagents can launch child subagents to create a tree of coordinated work. The main agent and its direct subagents can launch subagents, but a subagent launched by another subagent can't launch further ones.\\nNested launches also need Task tool access in the current mode, and hooks or tool policies can block spawning.\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$Lc1\",\"How do I see what a subagent is doing?\",{\"value\":\"How do I see what a subagent is doing?\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lc2\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"How do I see what a subagent is doing?\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"$Lc3\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Background subagents write output to \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-sm border border-border bg-card/80 p-1 font-mono text-xs\",\"children\":\"~/.cursor/subagents/\"}],\". The parent agent can read these files to check progress.\"]}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$Lc1\",\"What happens if a subagent fails?\",{\"value\":\"What happens if a subagent fails?\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lc2\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"What happens if a subagent fails?\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"$Lc3\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"The subagent returns an error status to the parent agent. The parent can retry, resume with additional context, or handle the failure differently.\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$Lc1\",\"Can I use MCP tools in subagents?\",{\"value\":\"Can I use MCP tools in subagents?\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lc2\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Can I use MCP tools in subagents?\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"$Lc3\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base mb-4 leading-relaxed!\",\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"Yes. Subagents inherit all tools from the parent, including MCP tools from configured servers. \",[\"$\",\"$L26\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"#cloud-subagents\",\"children\":\"Cloud subagents\"}],\" are the exception: they run on a cloud VM and use the MCP servers configured for your team at \",[\"$\",\"$Lbe\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline decoration-neutral-600 underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:decoration-neutral-700\",\"href\":\"https://cursor.com/agents\",\"children\":\"cursor.com/agents\"}],\", not the servers from your local session.\"]}]}]]}],\"$Lc4\",\"$Lc5\",\"$Lc6\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"b1:[\"$\",\"$Lc7\",null,{}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"b2:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"hidden xl:block w-64 px-4 pt-8\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lc8\",null,{\"headings\":[{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"How subagents work\",\"id\":\"how-subagents-work\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Foreground vs background\",\"id\":\"foreground-vs-background\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Built-in subagents\",\"id\":\"built-in-subagents\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Why these subagents exist\",\"id\":\"why-these-subagents-exist\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"When to use subagents\",\"id\":\"when-to-use-subagents\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Quick start\",\"id\":\"quick-start\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Custom subagents\",\"id\":\"custom-subagents\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"File locations\",\"id\":\"file-locations\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"File format\",\"id\":\"file-format\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Configuration fields\",\"id\":\"configuration-fields\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Model configuration\",\"id\":\"model-configuration\"},{\"level\":4,\"text\":\"Model parameters\",\"id\":\"model-parameters\"},{\"level\":4,\"text\":\"When the configured model won't be used\",\"id\":\"when-the-configured-model-wont-be-used\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Parent model and usage pools\",\"id\":\"parent-model-and-usage-pools\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Using subagents\",\"id\":\"using-subagents\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Automatic delegation\",\"id\":\"automatic-delegation\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Explicit invocation\",\"id\":\"explicit-invocation\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Parallel execution\",\"id\":\"parallel-execution\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Isolated project copies\",\"id\":\"isolated-project-copies\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Cloud subagents\",\"id\":\"cloud-subagents\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Start a cloud subagent with /in-cloud\",\"id\":\"start-a-cloud-subagent-with-in-cloud\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Put a PR on autopilot with /autopilot\",\"id\":\"put-a-pr-on-autopilot-with-autopilot\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Resuming subagents\",\"id\":\"resuming-subagents\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Common patterns\",\"id\":\"common-patterns\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Verification agent\",\"id\":\"verification-agent\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Orchestrator pattern\",\"id\":\"orchestrator-pattern\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Example subagents\",\"id\":\"example-subagents\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Debugger\",\"id\":\"debugger\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Test runner\",\"id\":\"test-runner\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Best practices\",\"id\":\"best-practices\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Anti-patterns to avoid\",\"id\":\"anti-patterns-to-avoid\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Managing subagents\",\"id\":\"managing-subagents\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Creating subagents\",\"id\":\"creating-subagents\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Viewing subagents\",\"id\":\"viewing-subagents\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"Performance and cost\",\"id\":\"performance-and-cost\"},{\"level\":3,\"text\":\"Token and cost considerations\",\"id\":\"token-and-cost-considerations\"},{\"level\":2,\"text\":\"FAQ\",\"id\":\"faq\"}],\"showCopyPageButton\":true,\"collapsible\":false}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"b6:[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":